<title>JAPAN: Japan passes on 20,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</title>
<headline>Japan passes on 20,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it had passed on 20,000 tonnes of Australian prime hard wheat and 20,000 of feed barley from North America at Thursday's weekly import tender.</p>
<p>The agency said it passed on the Australian wheat because selling prices from the Australian Wheat Board were higher than originally expected.</p>
</text>
